# variants/desktop/portage/package.use/36-x-compat — the X pieces a Wayland-only
# desktop still needs (D24, 2026-09-26). The base forces USE="-X"; there is no X
# session anywhere. Each line below is a library or client that has no Wayland-
# only build, found one at a time as the resolver reported it, with the reason.

# virtual/opengl-8 RDEPENDs on media-libs/libglvnd[X] -- the GLX dispatch -- for
# EVERY OpenGL consumer. So long as anything uses `opengl`, libglvnd carries its
# X client side (libX11, libXext). Libraries only: no server, no session.
media-libs/libglvnd X

# vlc-4 builds its VA-API output only against X: REQUIRED_USE "vaapi? ( X )".
# Off for vlc alone -- it still decodes in hardware through ffmpeg's VA-API.
media-video/vlc -vaapi

# --- X-only applications (author's decision, 2026-09-26): enable X on each one's
# toolkit rather than drop the app. Still no X session and no Xorg -- the apps run
# under XWayland, which the compositors already pull in.

# Plasma: libplasma and KWin's XWayland support require the X side of Qt, of
# KWindowSystem and of xkbcommon. OBS Studio needs qtbase[X] as well.
dev-qt/qtbase X
kde-frameworks/kwindowsystem X
x11-libs/libxkbcommon X

# Audacity (wxWidgets): wxGTK[X] -> gtk+[X] -> cairo[X], libepoxy[X].
# Wine -> gst-plugins-nvcodec -> nvidia-drivers also needs gtk+[X].
x11-libs/wxGTK X
x11-libs/gtk+ X
x11-libs/cairo X
media-libs/libepoxy X

# VirtualBox: its frontend and its SDL dependency are X-only.
app-emulation/virtualbox X
media-libs/libsdl2 X

# Consumers that depend on the toolkits above with [X=]: once the toolkit has X,
# they must match it (mkvtoolnix -> qtmultimedia; inkscape -> gtkmm -> cairomm;
# gimp -> gegl[sdl] -> libsdl-1.2).
dev-qt/qtmultimedia X
dev-cpp/gtkmm X
dev-cpp/cairomm X
media-libs/libsdl X
